  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24269648
    description: Version DOI of v0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A controlled comparison in Kimi Linear's hybrid layout (three Kimi Delta Attention layers, then one full attention
  layer, repeated six times): the softmax in the six attention layers is replaced by dilution attention, a
  parameter-free causal attention operator. Both models have 208,514,136 parameters and are trained with no position
  encoding at a 16K context on 4.19B FineWeb-Edu tokens, three seeds each, under the published DilutionAttention
  recipe. The repository holds the KDA layer, the configurations, run records, and evaluations of held-out loss,
  needle-in-a-haystack retrieval out to 256K tokens, harder retrieval with natural filler and keyed distractors,
  long-document loss on PG-19, the use of distant context, and attention on the needle.
